 "cards": [
  {
   "dot": "cyan",
   "title": "The Loop Contract",
   "items": [
    "One step is one brain call, exactly one tool call, one observation",
    "The cap is 8 steps; an activity retry does not consume a step, a malformed decision does",
    "The 6-minute ceiling sums per-step work, each step capped at 2 minutes, minus the human wait",
    "The brain is stateless: the transcript is the whole state",
    "Four ways to end: concluded, budget_exhausted, no_progress, failed"
   ]
  },
  {
   "dot": "violet",
   "title": "The Brain",
   "items": [
    "brain_decide asks ollama for deepseek-v4.1-flash:cloud",
    "AGENT_FALLBACK=on always runs the deterministic scripted policy",
    "AGENT_FALLBACK=auto uses the model and falls back when it is unreachable",
    "AGENT_FALLBACK=off uses the model only and fails the run when it is down"
   ]
  },
  {
   "dot": "amber",
   "title": "The Six Tools",
   "items": [
    "read_registry - versions and the stage that serves",
    "read_run_metrics - the run's own recorded metrics",
    "evaluate_version - scores a version against the incumbent",
    "train_candidate - trains a candidate; a repeat is idempotent",
    "propose_promotion - files the durable promotion and waits",
    "conclude - ends the run with an answer"
   ]
  },
  {
   "dot": "rose",
   "title": "The Human Gate",
   "items": [
    "propose_promotion files PromotionWorkflow through the promotion_outcome activity",
    "Approve promotes in the MLflow registry of record and routing moves traffic",
    "Decline completes with promoted: false; traffic does not move",
    "Terminate the promotion while the agent waits and the run records a failure",
    "Promotion and rollback both check the artifact before traffic moves"
   ]
  },
  {
   "dot": "emerald",
   "title": "Durability",
   "items": [
    "Kill the worker and the run resumes from its event history",
    "An interrupted activity is retried, so it runs again (at-least-once)",
    "The console shows the frozen step with a running clock: frozen, not lost",
    "schedule_to_start_timeout is bounded at 10 minutes; unbounded, a task stranded on a dead worker hangs for ever",
    "That timeout counts as a failed attempt, so too tight a bound turns a short outage into a dead run"
   ]
  }
 ]
